o prime.\n\n47: Same. sqrt(47)\u22486.8. Check 2,3,5. 47/2=23.5, 47/3\u224815.666, 47/5=9.4. So prime.\n\n57: 3\u00d719. Not prime.\n\n67: sqrt(67)\u22488.1. Check primes up to 7. 2,3,5,7. 67/7\u22489.571. Not divisible. So prime.\n\n77: 7\u00d711. Not prime.\n\n87: 3\u00d729. Not prime.\n\n97: sqrt(97)\u22489.8. Check primes up to 9. So 2,3,5,7. 97 not divisible by any. So prime.\n\nSo 6 primes in total. So the answer is C. Therefore, I think the correct option is C)6.", "deepseek_solution": "To determine the number of prime numbers less than 100 with a units digit of 7, we first list all such numbers:  \n**7, 17, 27, 37, 47, 57, 67, 77, 87, 97**.  \n\nNext, we check each for primality:  \n- **7**: Prime (divisors: 1, 7).  \n- **17**: Prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5, or 7).  \n- **27**: Not prime (divisible by 3).  \n- **37**: Prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5).  \n- **47**: Prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5).  \n- **57**: Not prime (divisible by 3).  \n- **67**: Prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5, 7).  \n- **77**: Not prime (divisible by 7).  \n- **87**: Not prime (divisible by 3).  \n- **97**: Prime (not divisible by 2, 3, 5, 7).  \n\n**Prime numbers identified**: 7, 17, 37, 47, 67, 97.  \n**Total**: 6 primes.  \n\n**Answer**: (C) 6.", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. We begin by identifying all prime numbers ending in the digit 7 that are less than 100.\n\n2. The prime numbers ending in 7 are:\n   \\[\n   7, 17, 37, 47, 67, 97\n   \\]\n\n3. Now, we count the number of such prime numbers:\n   \\[\n   7, 17, 37, 47, 67, 97 \\quad \\text{(six numbers)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Thus, the number of prime numbers less than 100 that end with the digit 7 is clearly 6.\n\n    Therefore, the correct choice is:\n\\[ \n\\boxed{6}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Consider the permutation of $1, 2, \\cdots, 20$ as $\\left(a_{1} a_{2} \\cdots a_{20}\\right)$. Perform the following operation on this permutation: swap the posi